---
import Layout from '../../layouts/WorkLayout.astro';
import Lottie from '../../components/Lottie.astro';

const meta = {
  title: "Designed a budget management feature with an adoption rate of one-third of active users – ysabella nicole alvarez",
  description: "Cashmonki was first introduced as a simple expense tracker where users can add and track transactions manually or automatically by scanning receipts. In this study, Ysabella explores implementing a feature that provides users with more insight and clarity into their spending habits.",
  ogImage: '/opengraph.png'
};

const src = "https://assets.ysabella.me";

const data = {
  status: 'shipped' as const,
  headline: "Designed a budget management feature with an adoption rate of one-third of active users.",
  subline: "Studies have shown that 60% of people don’t really know how much they spent the month before. Cashmonki was first introduced as a simple expense tracker where users can add and track transactions manually or by scanning and automatically parsing receipts.",
  details: [
    { label: "Product", value: "iOS mobile application" },
    { label: "Role", value: "Product designer"},
    { label: "Timeline", value: ["November 2025 -", "December 2025"]},
    { label: "Contribution", value: ["Experience design", "Market research", "Feature development"] }    
  ],
  subheadings: [
    { depth: 2, text: "problem", slug: "problem" },
    // { depth: 2, text: "research", slug: "research" },
    { depth: 2, text: "testing", slug: "testing" },
    { depth: 2, text: "outcome", slug: "outcome" },
    { depth: 2, text: "reflections", slug: "reflections" },
  ]
}

---
<Layout metadata={meta} data={data} >
  <div class="row lg wrap">
    <div class="card grid phone">
      <figure class="mockup column">
        <video class="screen" src=`${src}/work/cashmonki/manual.mp4` preload="none" autoplay="visible" muted loop playsinline />
        <figcaption class="small horizontal center">Manual entry</ficaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <div class="card grid phone">
      <figure class="mockup column">
        <video class="screen" src=`${src}/work/cashmonki/automatic.mp4` preload="none" autoplay="visible" muted loop playsinline />
        <figcaption class="small horizontal center">Automatic entry</ficaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
  <section class="column sm" id="problem">
    <div class="column xs">
      <header>
         <h3 class="caption label">Problem</h3>
          <h2 class="title">What does it mean to set a budget?</h2>
      </header>
      <p>While mapping out specifications to expand our simple expense tracker's functionality, we realized that “budget management” meant something different to everyone. For example, our lead tends to focus on short-term, goal-based budgets, whereas my preference leans towards viewing long-term expenditures and saving patterns.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="row lg">
      <figure class="card lg stretch">
        <div class="comparison">
          <div class="item">
            <div class="overlap">
              <figcaption class="small horizontal center">Short-term</figcaption>
              <div class="circle">
                <span id="plane">✈️</span>
                <span id="coffee">☕</span>
                <span id="food">🍕</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <span id="middle" class="caption label">?</span>
          <div class="item">
            <div class="overlap end">
              <figcaption class="small horizontal center">Long-term</figcaption>
              <div class="circle">
                <span id="house">🏠</span>
                <span id="car">🚗</span>
                <span id="college">🎓</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>
  <!-- <section class="column sm" id="research">
    <div class="column xs">
      <header>
         <h3 class="caption label">Research</h3>
          <h2 class="title">Similar apps don’t offer flexibility.</h2>
      </header>
      <p>A competitive analysis revealed that most budgeting features are locked into monthly cycles, offering little to no flexibility. I wanted users to be able to define budgets on their own terms: daily, weekly, or long-term.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="row lg">
      <figure class="card lg">
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section> -->
  <section class="column" id="testing">
    <div class="column xs">
      <header>
         <h3 class="caption label">Testing</h3>
          <h2 class="title">Iteration, iteration, iteration...</h2>
      </header>
      <p>To support different financial goals, I explored budgeting across adjustable time ranges rather than a single fixed cycle.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="column lg">
      <div class="row wrap lg end">
        <div class="card grid">
          <figure class="card lg">
            <Lottie 
              src=`${src}/work/cashmonki/iteration.json``
              loop={true}
              autoplay={true}
            />
          </figure>
        </div>
        <div class="content sm">
          <h4>So iterate I did.</h4>
          <p>In early explorations, I was met with the concern that although granularity would be nice to have in theory, there was the risk of introducing too much complexity.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="row wrap lg end">
        <div class="card grid">
          <figure class="mockup">
            <video class="screen" src=`${src}/work/cashmonki.mp4` preload="none" autoplay="visible" muted loop playsinline />
          </figure>
        </div>
        <div class="content sm">
          <h4>Eventually...</h4>
          <p>I simplified my approach: budgets are manageable directly from the dashboard, applied only to expenses and not income for the time being, and recur over a selected period of time.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="column sm" id="outcome">
    <div class="column xs">
      <header>
         <h3 class="caption label">Outcome</h3>
          <h2 class="title">A fully adaptable budget management feature.</h2>
      </header>
      <p>A key challenge I realized was translating budgets across different timeframes. For example, what would a daily budget look like on a weekly or monthly basis? To address this, we implemented adaptive calculations that preserve context across different periods.</p>
      <p>Although Cashmonki’s budgeting feature is optional and usage is inherently intentional, early launch data shows meaningful engagement with an estimated adoption rate of up to 30% in the first thirty days following launch.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="card lg note" id="reflections">
    <h3 class="caption label">Reflections</h3>
    <div class="row start wrap lg">
      <div class="column xs">
        <h4>Clarify the objective early.</h4>
        <p class="subtle">We had to pull the emergency brake during the iteration process to clarify goals and identify where experiences diverged. This helped me move forward with a solution that worked for multiple perspectives.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="column xs">
        <h4>Scale down to the MVP.</h4>
        <p class="subtle">This project pushed me to balance thoughtful functionality with practical simplicity by scaling down to the minimum viable product (MVP)—enabling my team to ship quickly and gather insights ASAP.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .card.grid:hover .mockup {
    transform: unset;
  }

  .comparison {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    width: 100%;
  }

  .comparison .item {
    display: flex;
    flex-grow: 1;
    flex-direction: column;
    max-width: none;
  }

  .overlap {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-self: flex-start;
    align-self: flex-start;
    gap: var(--size-padding-sm);
    width: 120%;
    height: 100%;
  }
  
  .overlap.end {
    justify-self: flex-end;
    align-self: flex-end;
  }

  .circle {
    flex-grow: 1;
    position: relative;
    aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
    border-radius: 100%;
    border: 1px dashed var(--color-border-2nd);

    span {
      position: absolute;
      font-size: calc(var(--size-heading-lg) * 1.5);
    }
  }

  #plane {
    top: 12%;
    left: 40%;
  }

  #coffee {
    top: 40%;
    left: 18%;
  }

  #food {
    top: 68%;
    left: 40%;
  }

  #house {
    top: 12%;
    right: 35%;
  }

  #car {
    top: 35%;
    right: 18%;
  }

  #college {
    top: 65%;
    right: 30%;
  }

  #middle {
    margin-top: var(--size-padding-lg);
    font-size: var(--size-type-body);
  }
</style>